# LINE ENDINGS
#
# `.prettierrc` sets endOfLine: "crlf", but nothing enforced it, so 59 of the 191 source
# files had drifted to LF or to a mix of both. That was 7,616 lint errors — 91% of this
# package's entire lint run — saying nothing whatever about the code, and drowning the
# ~780 findings that do.
#
# Without this file the answer depends on each machine's core.autocrlf, which means a
# fresh clone can reintroduce the whole problem. eol=crlf pins it for every checkout on
# every platform, so the working tree always matches what Prettier is configured to want.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# The exception, which must stay LF wherever it runs: render-build.sh is executed by
# Render's Linux builder, and CRLF makes the shebang unusable.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Never touched, never diffed.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
